# Production secrets — never committed.
#
# The whole directory, with NO tracked .gitkeep. It is a bind-mount source that must be
# owned by postgres (uid 999) inside the db container, and git on the box runs as the ssh
# user — a tracked file in there means git needs write on a directory it does not own, and
# `git reset --hard` in the deploy fails with `unable to unlink old
# 'ops/backups/.gitkeep': Permission denied`. Measured: that is exactly how deploy
# 30672150324 died. Docker creates the directory if it is absent and the db entrypoint
# chowns it, so nothing needs to keep the path alive in the tree.
ops/backups/
